    description: "PR 6 of the ADR-0003-ext (Linker Subcategory Restoration) rollout. Non-governance PRs 1-5 already merged: the new ADR, docs/LINKERS.md rewrite, docs/hypergumbo-spec.md and four ADR in-place corrections, and the 45-file module-docstring sweep with README/ARCHITECTURE/CHANGELOG updates.\n\nThis item is the one remaining PR and it touches governance files per AGENTS.md:\n\nPROPOSED EDITS:\n\n1. .agent/agent_playbooks_protocols_sops_skills/bakeoff-broad-priorities.md\n   - Line 5 priority #3: rewrite \"Linkers: polyglot repos are common and challenging for new developers; they are an opportunity for hypergumbo to shine\" as:\n     \"Linkers: post-call-graph-time edge recovery in four subcategories (Protocol / Bridge / Framework / Infrastructure — see ADR-0003-ext). Prioritize by expected FP-reduction volume per the prospector corpus (INV-nimuj), not by novelty of language pair.\"\n   - Line 6 priority #4 \"Frameworks\": reframe to note the interplay with Framework-subcategory linkers.\n\n2. .agent/agent_playbooks_protocols_sops_skills/bakeoff-deep-priorities.md\n   - Line 10 priority #7: same rewrite as BROAD above.\n\n3. .agent/agent_playbooks_protocols_sops_skills/trackerize-playbook.md\n   - Line 57 well-known tags list: add 'protocol_linkers', 'framework_dispatch_linkers', 'infrastructure_linkers' alongside the existing 'cross_language_linkers' (preserved for backwards continuity).\n\n4. AGENTS.md\n   - Add a short paragraph under \"Required Checks\" citing ADR-0003-ext as the authoritative linker subcategory definition and INV-nimuj as the prioritization heuristic.\n   - No change to BROAD/DEEP priority description lines (line 31, 34, 64, 67) — they already correctly mention 'linker' and 'framework' as paired concepts; once ADR-0003-ext is in effect the reader understands Framework linkers are a subcategory.\n\nRATIONALE:\nThe ADR-0003 §2.4 linker subcategory taxonomy (Protocol / Bridge / Framework, extended by ADR-0003-ext with Infrastructure) has been inert in working diction since 2026-01-07. The BROAD/DEEP playbooks' current phrasing treats 'linker' and 'framework' as parallel priorities, reinforcing the split that led to under-investing in within-language framework-dispatch linkers (see INV-nimuj and the WI-tubot 2026-04-11 prospector data). This edit aligns the playbook with the restored taxonomy.\n\nAwaiting approval before opening the PR. No code changes until this tracker item moves out of needs_human_review."  # 8728
